{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_476544259#1_977140301","relevance":3,"reason":"This document is dedicated to 1990s American pop culture history and directly describes entertainment in the decade, including gangsta rap's cultural impact, popular sports, many TV shows and sitcoms such as Seinfeld, movies such as Pulp Fiction, and music such as Radiohead.","learned":"A 1990s American pop-culture history source characterizes the decade as having influential gangsta rap, increasingly popular sports, many TV shows and sitcoms, major movies like Pulp Fiction, and prominent music acts like Radiohead."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1949","reason":"This query produced a strong grade-3 American pop-culture history result, so continuing is likely to find more directly relevant 1990s U.S. entertainment evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1949"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_538874050#15_1231688808","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1949","rank":2,"snippet":"and West Coast 4. The Harry Potter Series 5. The Titanic 6. The Girl Bands 7. The Friends 8. The King of Pop 9. Fast Food 10. The TAMAGOTCHIS Pet 11. The FUBU Street Wear 12. Home Alone 13. The Macarena Dance Movement Conclusion \" , \"segment\": \"It was played in clubs, weddings, proms, and other events, making it a great 90's pop culture dance. Conclusion Can you say that the 90s was one of the best decades? The '90s is an unforgettable moment for the evolution of American pop culture. Most of the older millennials can well remember these and many more popular culture of the 1990s. What was your favorite pop culture? I bet you can write a great essay on video games from the '90s, the funny sitcoms, great <cover>music, and so much more. We also hope you had fun remembering the famous catchphrases from the 90's pop culture.\" , \"start_char\": 5718.000000 , \"title\": \"American Pop Culture in the 1990s</cover>\" , \"url\": \"https://www.throwbacks.com/american-pop-culture-in-the-1990s/\" }"}}
