{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1949"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_1666935558#7_3415733531","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1949","rank":7,"snippet":"Popular? Kpop in Television Why is Kpop Unique? What is the Hallyu Wave and how does it relate to Kpop? How to Become a Kpop Idol? How to Get into Kpop? Learn to Read Korean in 90 Minutes – FREE! 22 replies to \"What is Kpop? Here is everything you need to know\" \" , \"segment\": \"Kpop is considered a fairly new form of music. The type of K-Pop music that you’re listening to today was formed around the <cover>1990s. The roots for K-Pop began from the 1950s, however, and have since then already been influenced a lot by different types of Western music and pop groups. American pop culture </cover>has especially had – and still does have – an effect on K-Pop. What was the very first Kpop group? Unlike other musical genres, contemporary Kpop start can be pinpointed to a certain date: April 11th of 1992, when the groups Seo Taiji and The Boys performed their music on TV for the first time. They were active in the mid-1990s and were known for experimenting with many different genres of music. For example, they were the pioneers for integrating rap into South Korean ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_1095086771#5_2064172607","rank":5,"relevance":1},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_538874050#0_1231667568","rank":6,"relevance":3}]}}
